---
// Consumer-side vs producer-side interfaces and returning structs (#6, #7).
const W = 900;
const H = 372;

function arrow(x1: number, y1: number, x2: number, y2: number) {
  const a = Math.atan2(y2 - y1, x2 - x1);
  const len = 8;
  const p1 = [x2 - len * Math.cos(a - 0.45), y2 - len * Math.sin(a - 0.45)];
  const p2 = [x2 - len * Math.cos(a + 0.45), y2 - len * Math.sin(a + 0.45)];
  return {
    line: `M ${x1} ${y1} L ${x2 - 6 * Math.cos(a)} ${y2 - 6 * Math.sin(a)}`,
    head: `${x2},${y2} ${p1[0].toFixed(1)},${p1[1].toFixed(1)} ${p2[0].toFixed(1)},${p2[1].toFixed(1)}`,
  };
}

// Top: consumers depend on a fat producer interface (and returning a consumer interface creates a cycle)
const t1 = arrow(486, 68, 360, 82);
const t2 = arrow(486, 128, 360, 114);
const tCyc = arrow(360, 98, 486, 98);

// Bottom: consumers depend only on concrete types; zero reverse edges from store
const b1 = arrow(464, 268, 330, 286);
const b2 = arrow(464, 328, 330, 312);
---
<figure class="gp12b">
  <div class="gp12b-scroll">
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Top: a producer-side interface forces every caller to mock unused methods, and returning a consumer interface creates an import cycle. Bottom: the producer returns concrete *Store while each consumer declares only the small interface it uses.">
    {/* Top panel */}
    <text x="20" y="26" class="h">
      <tspan data-lang-en>1. Producer owns the interface (coupling) or returns a consumer interface (cycle)</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>1. Bên cung cấp ôm sẵn interface (dính chùm) hoặc trả về interface của bên gọi (vòng lặp)</tspan>
    </text>

    <rect x="20" y="44" width="336" height="108" rx="6" class="hot" />
    <text x="36" y="68" class="b">package store</text>
    <text x="36" y="92" class="m">type CustomerStorage interface</text>
    <text x="36" y="114" class="m">Get, ListAll, Update, Delete, ...</text>
    <text x="36" y="136" class="r">
      <tspan data-lang-en>fat contract forced on every caller</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>ép mọi bên gọi gánh đủ mọi method</tspan>
    </text>

    <g><path d={t1.line} class="lnr" /><polygon points={t1.head} class="arr" /></g>
    <g><path d={t2.line} class="lnr" /><polygon points={t2.head} class="arr" /></g>
    <g><path d={tCyc.line} class="lnr dash" /><polygon points={tCyc.head} class="arr" /></g>

    <rect x="490" y="44" width="390" height="48" rx="6" class="box" />
    <text x="506" y="65" class="b">package billing</text>
    <text x="506" y="83" class="m">
      <tspan data-lang-en>uses Get only, must mock 6 methods</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>chỉ gọi Get, vẫn phải mock cả 6 method</tspan>
    </text>

    <rect x="490" y="104" width="390" height="48" rx="6" class="box" />
    <text x="506" y="125" class="b">package reporting</text>
    <text x="506" y="143" class="m">
      <tspan data-lang-en>uses ListAll only, breaks on new methods</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>chỉ gọi ListAll, dễ vỡ khi store thêm method</tspan>
    </text>

    <text x="20" y="176" class="r">
      <tspan data-lang-en>Dashed arrow: if store returns an interface owned by billing, Go rejects the import cycle.</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Mũi tên đứt: nếu store trả về interface đặt bên billing, Go báo lỗi import vòng tròn.</tspan>
    </text>

    <line x1="20" x2={W - 20} y1="198" y2="198" class="rule" />

    {/* Bottom panel */}
    <text x="20" y="226" class="h">
      <tspan data-lang-en>2. Producer returns *Store; each consumer discovers the tiny interface it needs</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>2. Bên cung cấp trả *Store; mỗi bên gọi tự khai báo interface nhỏ cho riêng mình</tspan>
    </text>

    <rect x="20" y="244" width="306" height="108" rx="6" class="box" />
    <text x="36" y="268" class="b">package store</text>
    <text x="36" y="292" class="m">func New() *Store</text>
    <text x="36" y="314" class="m">Get(...), ListAll(...), Update(...)</text>
    <text x="36" y="336" class="b">
      <tspan data-lang-en>zero imports of any consumer</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>không hề import bất kỳ bên gọi nào</tspan>
    </text>

    <g><path d={b1.line} class="ln" /><polygon points={b1.head} class="ar" /></g>
    <g><path d={b2.line} class="ln" /><polygon points={b2.head} class="ar" /></g>

    <rect x="468" y="244" width="412" height="48" rx="6" class="box" />
    <text x="484" y="265" class="b">package billing</text>
    <text x="484" y="283" class="m">type customerGetter interface {'{ Get(id) }'}</text>

    <rect x="468" y="304" width="412" height="48" rx="6" class="box" />
    <text x="484" y="325" class="b">package reporting</text>
    <text x="484" y="343" class="m">type customerLister interface {'{ ListAll() }'}</text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Arrows show package imports. Because Go interfaces are satisfied implicitly, <code>*store.Store</code> satisfies both tiny consumer interfaces without <code>store</code> importing <code>billing</code> or <code>reporting</code>.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Mũi tên thể hiện chiều import package. Nhờ interface khớp ngầm định, <code>*store.Store</code> tự đáp ứng cả hai interface nhỏ bên gọi mà <code>store</code> không cần import <code>billing</code> hay <code>reporting</code>.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .gp12b { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .gp12b-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .gp12b svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; }
  .gp12b text { font-size: 13.5px; fill: var(--text-body); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .gp12b .h { font-size: 15.5px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gp12b .b { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gp12b .m { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 13px; }
  .gp12b .r { fill: var(--red); font-weight: 700; font-size: 13px; }
  .gp12b .box { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .gp12b .hot { fill: var(--red-tint-bg); stroke: var(--red); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .gp12b .ln { fill: none; stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .gp12b .ar { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .gp12b .lnr { fill: none; stroke: var(--red); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .gp12b .lnr.dash { stroke-dasharray: 4 3; }
  .gp12b .arr { fill: var(--red); }
  .gp12b .rule { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; }
  .gp12b figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
